{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1908","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1908","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1908\",\"parent_revision\":\"2a4d155a43bbc778fa696cb970f5d18bac764077ed68e82ddfd2ded4afb0e3d1\",\"root_revision\":\"2a4d155a43bbc778fa696cb970f5d18bac764077ed68e82ddfd2ded4afb0e3d1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-02\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **plugin-assessor: does not fetch source: urls to detect drift between skill content and cited upstream references** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-04-23 drift audit revealed assessor performs structural audit only; upstream URL checking was manual\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Condition | Classification | Notes |\\n|-----------|---------------|-------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Detect drift between SOURCE: claims and upstream via URL fetch |\\n| Target agent to modify | AVAILABLE | plugins/plugin-creator/agents/plugin-assessor.md \u2014 61 lines, no URL fetching present |\\n| SOURCE: URL pattern | AVAILABLE | Pattern SOURCE: [Title](URL) (accessed YYYY-MM-DD) defined in CLAUDE.md citation requirements |\\n| Integration point in assessment phases | DERIVABLE | Phase 3 (Skills Analysis) and Phase 5 (Agents Analysis) are natural insertion points |\\n| Output format for drift findings | DERIVABLE | Follows existing CRITICAL/WARNING/RECOMMENDATION structure |\\n| Drift threshold | MISSING | Not defined \u2014 needed before implementation |\\n| Unreachable URL handling policy | MISSING | No policy defined; 4xx vs timeout need different severity treatment |\\n| Rate-limit / timeout policy for URL fetching | MISSING | Not defined \u2014 needed to prevent assessment hangs |\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the assessor processes a skill file containing SOURCE: citations with URLs: each URL is fetched; the content surrounding the SOURCE: marker is compared to the fetched upstream content; discrepancies are reported as DRIFT findings at appropriate severity; unreachable URLs are flagged separately rather than silenced; URL fetch failures do not block the rest of the assessment.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nRunning plugin-assessor on a plugin with SOURCE: citations produces a Citation Drift sub-section in the assessment report. Each SOURCE: URL is listed with: fetch status, drift detected (yes/no), and finding text when drift is present. Items with drift appear in the Action Items section with file:line references. Plugins with zero SOURCE: citations produce no error \u2014 the phase is skipped cleanly.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running plugin-assessor on plugins/plugin-creator produces a Citation Drift section in the assessment report when at least one SOURCE: URL is present in a skill file.\\n2. When a cited URL returns content that no longer contains the specific phrase cited in the skill, the assessor flags it as a DRIFT finding at WARNING or RECOMMENDATION severity with file:line reference.\\n3. When a cited URL is unreachable (4xx, timeout, DNS failure), the assessor reports it as Unreachable Citation \u2014 not as drift \u2014 with the URL and the reason.\\n4. When a cited URL is reachable and the cited content is still present, no drift finding is emitted for that citation.\\n5. Running the assessor on a plugin with zero SOURCE: citations produces no error and no empty drift section.\\n6. Each URL fetch has a configurable timeout; the assessor continues after timeout and records the URL as unreachable, not hung.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- What constitutes drift? Is substring absence of the cited phrase sufficient, or is structural/semantic comparison required?\\n- What is the maximum number of URLs the assessor should fetch per run (cost and latency bound)?\\n- When a URL is unreachable, should it be WARNING or silently skipped?\\n- Should GitHub-hosted URLs be exempt from fetching (already in-repo trust domain)?\\n- Should drift findings reduce the overall plugin score or appear only informational?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent | @plugin-creator:plugin-assessor \u2014 plugins/plugin-creator/agents/plugin-assessor.md |\\n| File | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/assessor/references/assessment-report-format.md |\\n| File | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/assessor/references/scoring-criteria.md |\\n| Related backlog | #1899 \u2014 skill-content-updater (upstream auto-sync, distinct but complementary) |\\n| Rule | CLAUDE.md \u2014 Citation Requirements section |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (self-contained change to plugin-assessor agent)\\n- Blocks: None directly; complements #1899\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Drift threshold policy not defined \u2014 what qualifies as drift must be specified before implementation\\n- Timeout and rate-limit policy not defined \u2014 needed to prevent assessment hangs\\n- WebFetch availability for plugin-assessor agent not confirmed \u2014 inherited tool set must be verified\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 URL extraction and reporting logic is well-scoped. Assuming substring match MVP: one agent file and two reference files. Semantic diff is a stretch goal.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/agents/plugin-assessor.md | New sub-step within Phase 3 (Skills Analysis) and Phase 5 (Agents Analysis) for SOURCE: URL drift detection |\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/skills/assessor/references/assessment-report-format.md | Add Citation Drift section to report template |\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/skills/assessor/references/scoring-criteria.md | Define how drift findings affect Documentation Quality score |\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nURL extraction: Parse SOURCE: markers from skill content. Canonical form: SOURCE: [Title](URL) (accessed YYYY-MM-DD). Regex SOURCE:\\\\s+\\\\[([^\\\\]]+)\\\\]\\\\(([^)]+)\\\\) extracts the URL; surrounding 2-3 sentence context is the claim to verify.\\n\\nFetch approach: One WebFetch call per unique URL, with a timeout (threshold TBD). Deduplicate URLs across reference files to avoid redundant fetches.\\n\\nSeverity mapping:\\n- URL returns 404/410 \u2192 CRITICAL (source is gone; citation is broken)\\n- URL unreachable (timeout, DNS, 5xx) \u2192 WARNING (content may still be valid)\\n- Key phrase absent from fetched page \u2192 RECOMMENDATION (drift suspected; human review needed)\\n- URL reachable and phrase found \u2192 no finding\\n\\nInsertion point: Sub-step at end of Phase 3 (after reference file audit) and Phase 5 (after frontmatter validation). Both phases already read full file content; SOURCE: extraction runs on that content without re-reading.\\n\\nWebFetch must be confirmed available to plugin-assessor agent before implementation (agent frontmatter has no explicit tools: field).\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent running /plugin-creator:assessor on a plugin before marketplace submission, I want the assessor to fetch each SOURCE: URL cited in skill documentation and compare the cited claim against the live upstream content, so that I can detect when upstream docs have changed and the skill guidance has drifted \u2014 before that stale guidance misleads future agents.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `plugin-assessor` agent performs structural audit of plugin files (frontmatter schema, component paths, cross-references) but does not fetch the upstream URLs cited in `SOURCE:` references within skill and agent files. When a skill states `SOURCE: [Title](https://...) (accessed YYYY-MM-DD)`, that URL is the canonical source from which the skill content was derived. The assessor has no mechanism to detect when local content has drifted from what those URLs currently say.\\n\\n**Where observed**: During the 2026-04-23 drift audit, 9 upstream URLs were fetched manually and compared against plugin-creator skills. The audit found contradictions (e.g., `output-styles.md` had an absolute claim that upstream contradicted with a `keep-coding-instructions: true` flag), stale data (scheduled-tasks expiry wrong), and 20+ missing features. The `plugin-assessor` agent ran during that workflow but produced no upstream drift findings because it does not fetch URLs.\\n\\n**Impact**:\\n- Skills accumulate drift silently after initial authoring \u2014 SOURCE citations become stale without any assessment mechanism to detect it\\n- The assessor's quality score does not reflect accuracy against cited sources, only structural compliance\\n- Drift is only discovered when a human manually fetches each cited URL, which is what triggered this session\\n\\n**User-provided context** (design direction \u2014 not requirements):\\nSOURCE citations in skills are a contract: the skill claims to derive its content from that URL. Fetching and comparing against those URLs is part of assessing skill quality and accuracy. This capability belongs in the assessor so drift detection is automatic on every assessment run, not a manual per-session task.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"081fbbc0ffb4ab531bf168a2e9788f21ae940ac2d38db98cc0dfb74d0e68118a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCbOig\"}"}